<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.reads ~ what stands for a hand at the disk shore

The vessel looks at the disk first, so the list stands true to the bytes at that instant, then names every row the shore holds: each STANDOFF (the disk and the records say different things and nothing writes) with its key, and each PENDING REMOVAL (a file vanished where a base stands; nothing writes back and nothing tombstones). Both islands read as one shore, every page of each, each row naming its island (`wiki`, the active wiki's mirrors; `daemon`, the daemon wiki's and the crossroads). A bare `lares shore` lists.

`face=N` names a LIT SIBLING's shore by handle index: its own projector answers in the daemon island with no wear, and a face that stands no projection refuses `face-unprojected`. `--bag` narrows to one bag. The list refuses to state a shore nobody measured: rows with no count, a page with no mark, a cursor that stands still, or rows short of the counts refuse `shore-list-unpaged`, and a mark that moves mid-read refuses `shore-list-moved`. Where a commit took a pending removal's file from its checkout, the row names that commit beside it (short sha, subject, PR, and the ashes git keeps) as `retiredBy`.

A seat reads the shore through `shore`; the answers that settle a row stay a person's hand at a terminal, so a seat names the command for the operator.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ what-stands · a-siblings-shore · one-bag

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`what-stands` params=`~ list every standoff and pending removal`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-siblings-shore` params=`face/2 ~ read a lit sibling's shore without wearing it`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-bag` params=`bag/lares ~ narrow the list to one bag`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · bag

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ a lit sibling's shore, by handle index (a whole number from 0); its own projector answers with no wear`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug ~ narrow to one bag`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a read: the vessel looks at the disk and names what stands; it writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ face-malformed · face-unprojected · shore-list-unpaged · shore-list-moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-malformed` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads face/2]] ~ --face names a handle index, a whole number from 0`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-unprojected` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ the named face stands no projection; read the worn face's shore`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`shore-list-unpaged` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ the island answered an unpaged list, a page with no mark, or rows short of its counts; read it again`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`shore-list-moved` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ the island's shore moved while the read walked its pages; read it again`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

